confirm.description:
Home Assistant still lists {count} Ampio entities that the Ampio server serves to the administrator login alone. This integration uses a standard Ampio account:

{names}

They come back on their own, with the same entity ids, if you point the integration back at the administrator account. Submit deletes these records from Home Assistant instead. Automations and dashboards that name them stop working. Nothing changes on the Ampio server.

Home Assistant still lists {count} Ampio devices or entities that Ampio Designer no longer provides. They were deleted, or moved to another module:

{names}

Submit deletes these records from Home Assistant. Automations and dashboards that name them stop working. Nothing changes on the Ampio server. A moved object comes back under its new module after the reload that follows.

Home Assistant still lists {count} Ampio devices or entities that the Ampio account of this integration is not served:

{names}

If you deleted them in Ampio Designer, Submit deletes these records from Home Assistant. Automations and dashboards that name them stop working. Nothing changes on the Ampio server. If the account lost access to them, do not submit. Restore the access in the Ampio app, then reload the integration.
